Z||000000||Nyte||04-26-2001||02:41 AM||||Someone wrote...<P>"If you want to build a nice Iron Duke, then remember this: all of the stock Fiero dukes are at least 13 years old. A <B>thorough engine rebuild with 3 angle vavle job, mild cam, and a hooker header</B> will make a huge difference."<P>How much would that stuff cost, doing it yourself as much as possible?<P>------------------<BR><B>Matthew "Whyt Nyte" D.</B><BR><B><I>84 SE</B>- automatic, rare Fender Delete option "Fender gap?  What fender gap?"</I><P>"Damned '84 econo coupes!  Why didn't you guys tell me this BEFORE I bought the dang thing!"||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||04-26-2001||07:37 AM||||If it is truly an "econo-coupe" then you may have something the v-8 guys are all looking for.  The "econo-coupe" has the low gear ratio trans that works well with the power of the v-8s.  The 4spd Muncie in my 85SE v-6 has something like 3.63:1 ratio that makes first gear virtually useless for the v-8.  The "econo-coupe" has a ratio more like 3.3:1 or 2.90:1  or lower (don't know the exact ratio).  So don't feel bad about your car.<P>All Fieros are fun cars to drive when they are in healthy condition.||||reg||1
