Z||000010||EdsB52||04-29-2001||07:34 PM||||Your original post read;<P>"If you want to build a nice Iron Duke, then remember this: all of the stock Fiero dukes are at least 13 years old. A thorough engine rebuild with 3 angle vavle job, mild cam, and a hooker header will make a huge difference."<P>I believe someone did write 'huge difference'. But like everything, it's subject to perspective and it's also relative. Would you be going from gutless wonder to semi-gutless wonder? What hp gain if any do you expect to realize with a 3 angle valve job? I've had 3 4cyl Fieros plus my 87GT that I currently have. My opinion between the two is that the 4cyl was more fun to drive in many ways. I have my favorite freeway corners that blew through at 90+mph that I wouldn't take at much above 80 in my 6cyl.  You can feel the weight shift as you throw it into the corner and it feels uncertain. I imagine I could put struts and swaybars and maybe bigger tires, or maybe 16's on it, but that defeats the purpose of a Fiero in my mind. It's a 14yo car that's fun and economical to drive. I have a 94 Camaro Z-28, 6sp that I bought for 8 thou that does a better job of power and handling, that when I eventually sell it, can get a lot of my money out of. Whereas the Fiero w/all the toys would not yield most of.<P>Now, the power differences between the 4 and 6 are ovbious and possess great disparity. If I were to start over again, I would get an 86-88 4 cyl Fiero and throw in a quad-4 or some other fat 4 cyl eng.<P>So, to finally answer your question, a stock rebuild costs about $1,000 done right. I would estimate almost twice that for the stuff your talking about doing. How much would it cost to put in a quad 4? Do you have the facilities and ability to do the mod? To me, building the duke is like puting make-up and perfume on a whore. I don't think the potential is there. I recently rented and drove a Grand Am to L.Vegas. When we got gas in Kingman, I was thinking what a derated 6 cyl piece of crap I was driving, so I popped the hood and found a four cyl.  I looked in the owners manual and found it read 150 or 155 hp. I thought it was a gutless 6 banger before I knew it was a 4. And that was with an automatic. I wouldn't mind having that in my Fiero. ||||reg||1
